build container:
root folder:
docker build -t <myapp-name> .
other folder:
docker build -t test-flask-app ./basic_example

run container:
docker run --rm <myapp-name>
forward a port default for example for Flask:
docker run -p <port>:<port> <myapp-name>
docker run -d -p 50000:50000 test-flask-app

remove container:
get container id:
docker ps
remove:
docker rm -f <container_id_or_name>

remove container image:
get image id or name:
docker images
remove:
docker rmi -f <image_id_or_name>



All camands:
-------------------------------------------
Docker Images:
Show images:
docker images
Delete image:
docker rmi <image_id_or_name>
Force delete image:
docker image rm -f <image_id_or_name>

Docker Containers:
For stop:
docker stop <container_id_or_name>
Forced Kill:
docker kill <container_id_or_name>
Remove:
docker rm <container_id_or_name>